WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:01.775
- [Voiceover] Here.

00:00:03.815 --> 00:00:06.673
(playful music, featuring a trumpet)

00:00:09.484 --> 00:00:11.297
- Mars and I have been

00:00:11.297 --> 00:00:14.828
cat human buddies for
about five years now.

00:00:14.828 --> 00:00:17.409
He's just this, he's
the biggest stoner cat.

00:00:17.409 --> 00:00:20.257
He just loves to sit around, eat,

00:00:20.257 --> 00:00:21.729
he loves being in bags,

00:00:21.729 --> 00:00:23.569
I don't know what to say,
he just loves being in bags.

00:00:23.569 --> 00:00:25.137
- This is my cat Riceball,

00:00:25.137 --> 00:00:27.707
he's very friendly, he's
more like a dog cat,

00:00:27.707 --> 00:00:29.382
He like, he does not afraid of people,

00:00:29.382 --> 00:00:32.038
he doesn't scratch, or anything.

00:00:32.038 --> 00:00:33.595
No, he has never been outside before,

00:00:33.595 --> 00:00:35.415
but when I moved out to LA,

00:00:35.415 --> 00:00:37.943
I did brought him with me,

00:00:37.943 --> 00:00:41.100
but he's never been actually,
physically on the ground.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.746
- My name in Rocco, and I love cats.

00:00:43.746 --> 00:00:46.028
More than I could love anything else.

00:00:46.028 --> 00:00:47.884
My first adult job,

00:00:47.884 --> 00:00:50.924
being a cat care attendant at the SPCA,

00:00:50.924 --> 00:00:54.199
and moved into cat behavior specialist

00:00:54.199 --> 00:00:56.012
at the San Francisco SPCA.

00:00:56.012 --> 00:00:58.839
This guy is like, the most
special cat I've ever met.

00:00:58.839 --> 00:01:00.652
I just was realizing
that I wouldn't sell him

00:01:00.652 --> 00:01:02.050
for a million dollars.

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:04.023
I think the benefits of
walking a cat on a leash

00:01:04.023 --> 00:01:05.922
is that they do get that outdoor time,

00:01:05.922 --> 00:01:07.362
but then there's no chance that

00:01:07.362 --> 00:01:10.007
they're going to get mauled
or carried away by a coyote.

00:01:10.007 --> 00:01:12.172
I would say the first
piece of advice I have,

00:01:12.172 --> 00:01:16.706
not all cats are gonna take to a harness.

00:01:16.706 --> 00:01:18.615
- [Devin] Can you stay still for a second?

00:01:18.615 --> 00:01:20.033
Stay still. No.

00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:25.033
- So right now I'm trying
to put the leash on him.

00:01:25.046 --> 00:01:26.998
- I'm not hurting my cat, I promise,

00:01:26.998 --> 00:01:30.038
I'm just kind of making him do something

00:01:30.038 --> 00:01:31.809
that is good for him ultimately.

00:01:31.809 --> 00:01:33.668
- [Iris] Riceball thank you!

00:01:34.688 --> 00:01:35.946
But you have to come back!

00:01:35.946 --> 00:01:38.965
- If your cat freezes in the harness,

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.074
then you're going to have to work on

00:01:40.074 --> 00:01:42.218
its relationship to
being inside that harness

00:01:42.218 --> 00:01:43.861
before you can take it outside.

00:01:43.861 --> 00:01:45.952
- So, I had to call in backup,

00:01:45.952 --> 00:01:47.648
this is my roommate Abby,

00:01:47.648 --> 00:01:51.268
we are going to attempt
to put this on him.

00:01:52.597 --> 00:01:54.752
Yay, the harness is on!

00:01:54.752 --> 00:01:57.237
- Oh, but you look so cute in this!

00:01:57.237 --> 00:01:58.912
- He doesn't look happy, does he?

00:01:58.912 --> 00:02:00.809
- [Abby] No, no, that's not
a happy cat right there.

00:02:00.809 --> 00:02:02.728
- [Devin] He does not look happy.

00:02:02.728 --> 00:02:04.617
- Okay, I heard you.

00:02:04.617 --> 00:02:05.999
- The best advice with any type

00:02:05.999 --> 00:02:07.162
of behavioral issue with a cat

00:02:07.162 --> 00:02:10.128
is try to figure out
how to work with them.

00:02:10.128 --> 00:02:11.707
Because if it knows you want something,

00:02:11.707 --> 00:02:12.699
it's not going to do it.

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:14.534
So if you want them to do something,

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:16.816
then you're gonna have to
figure out how to trick them

00:02:16.816 --> 00:02:18.576
into thinking that they want it.

00:02:18.576 --> 00:02:23.195
- What is this? Look at it! Oh! Oh!

00:02:23.195 --> 00:02:24.223
He's walking with me!

00:02:24.223 --> 00:02:26.292
- Here we go!

00:02:26.292 --> 00:02:27.242
Let's try this.

00:02:27.242 --> 00:02:29.631
No, let's go this way.

00:02:29.631 --> 00:02:31.587
No, let's go this way.

00:02:31.587 --> 00:02:33.395
(Mars meows)

00:02:34.531 --> 00:02:36.249
Mars!

00:02:36.249 --> 00:02:37.667
- [Iris] Let's go, let's go.

00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:39.502
Let's go, treat!

00:02:39.502 --> 00:02:41.800
- [Devin] Mars, c'mon.

00:02:42.755 --> 00:02:44.531
C'mon baby.

00:02:45.699 --> 00:02:46.841
We're just gonna go,

00:02:46.841 --> 00:02:48.712
no, we're just gonna go on a little walk.

00:02:49.881 --> 00:02:54.474
- (laughing) Look at her!

00:02:59.961 --> 00:03:00.953
- He's stressing me out,

00:03:00.953 --> 00:03:03.139
I'm really, this is really stressful.

00:03:03.139 --> 00:03:04.697
This is very, very stressful.

00:03:04.697 --> 00:03:07.246
Uh, he's not liking this, at all.

00:03:07.246 --> 00:03:09.251
- Oh he's, he's doing
better than I thought.

00:03:09.251 --> 00:03:11.737
I thought he was just gonna,
like, sitting in one corner,

00:03:11.737 --> 00:03:13.006
and doesn't move at all.

00:03:13.006 --> 00:03:16.142
But he's making some kind of process.

00:03:16.142 --> 00:03:17.934
C'mon, let's go!

00:03:17.934 --> 00:03:21.113
- Mars is now wedged in
between my neighbors hedge

00:03:21.113 --> 00:03:22.371
and my front porch.

00:03:22.371 --> 00:03:25.827
- We probably walked, like,

00:03:25.827 --> 00:03:27.310
three steps out of apartment?

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:28.985
The apartment door is right there.

00:03:28.985 --> 00:03:32.537
- I just feel like maybe
this wasn't for him.

00:03:32.537 --> 00:03:36.974
Right? You wanna go back inside?

00:03:36.974 --> 00:03:39.086
- And cats, we're built to serve them.

00:03:39.086 --> 00:03:41.262
That's why the ancient
Egyptian's worshipped them,

00:03:41.262 --> 00:03:42.307
you know what I mean?

00:03:42.307 --> 00:03:45.081
I live to serve my cat, and that's honest.

00:03:45.081 --> 00:03:47.673
So, if he wants to go on a walk,

00:03:47.673 --> 00:03:50.088
I'm gonna provide that service.

